 "limitations": [
  "ANATOMICAL leg only: no row mask, no settle, no seed \u2014 this is wiring geometry and NOT an operating point (L164).",
  "Operator powers are walks WITH revisits, not paths.",
  "The Crofts/Estrada second leg is NOT run (PREREG-disclosed): the strength normalisation is not neutral under a substrate change, and L206 already reported it agrees in ORDER on f4wA.",
  "The cohorts differ in SIZE across substrates (58 / 34 / 35 present ladder cells), so a percentile has coarser resolution on the smaller ones (1/34 = 0.029).",
  "The mirror leg uses a MASS-MATCHED COHORT percentile, not the l169c degree-neutral rewire null that L206 used for the carrier; the two are different nulls and are never compared as if they were the same.",
  "The closure and cutwA substrates share one ladder (ng_desc, no syn floor) while f4wA has its own (ng4, syn>=4): each substrate is scored against the ladder it was derived with, which is why the carrier's slot differs (25 vs 21) \u2014 that difference IS the design, not a confound.",
  "Q3 is exploratory and structurally unanswerable on this volume pair."
 ],
